es: docs/reports/android-homescreen-widgets.md (new)","+  depends: TASK-2, TASK-3, TASK-4, TASK-5, TASK-6","+  risk: low. It is documentation only, with no build or runtime impact.","+","+## Unclear / for the maintainer","+","+- The brief has no \"Why\" and no \"Out of scope\". The analyst assumes the","+  report stays technology-agnostic about *which* widgets ship. It proposes","+  candidates and does not pick a final set.","+- It is unclear whether introducing Kotlin (needed for Glance) is acceptable","+  in this repo. The report should present this as a trade-off, not assume it.","+- It is unclear whether moving the auth token out of the WebView into native","+  storage is acceptable from a security/privacy standpoint. The report","+  should surface this as a decision for the maintainer."]}],"originalFile":"# Tasks: Audit: android homescreen widgets\n\nid: opinion\nanalyst:\ndate:\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Task breakdown\n\n<!-- TASK-1: description\n     files: list of files likely affected\n     depends: none\n     risk: low / medium / high — reason\n\nTASK-2: ...\n-->\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019ddkafi6v4vyggqRN5bXA5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg43CusMNjnJwGk492ptp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written the task list to `docs/jobs/opinion_audit-android-homescreen-widgets/tasks.md`. This is a report-only job, so the only output will be `docs/reports/android-homescreen-widgets.md`; there are no code, build or F-Droid changes. I couldn't run `git branch --show-current` here, so I read the worktree's git HEAD file instead; it points to `report/opinion_audit-android-homescreen-widgets`, which matches the brief.\n\n**Main finding:** a widget is drawn by Android itself, outside the app, so it can't read the WebView's browser storage. That's where the login token and its expiry date (`auth`) and the server address (`custom_api_url`) are kept. So the main design question is how a widget gets data at all. The report should compare three options:\n- **Snapshot:** the web app sends ready-made widget data to Android through a custom Capacitor plugin, the same way `PullToRefreshPlugin` connects the two today. The widget never contacts the server itself.\n- **Token handoff:** the token is copied into Android storage and the widget fetches data itself, including renewing the token when it expires. This has security implications.\n- **Shortcuts only:** widgets show no data and just open the app.\n\nTapping a widget could open a specific screen the same way shared text already opens `/share` in `MainActivity`.\n\n**Tasks:**\n1. **Current setup (low risk):** list what's already in place: Java vs. Kotlin, Gradle and Android SDK versions, Capacitor plugins, manifest.\n2. **Technical options (medium risk):** compare Android's built-in widget API (`AppWidgetProvider`/`RemoteViews`, no new dependencies), Jetpack Glance (needs Kotlin), and existing Capacitor widget plugins. Library status changes over time, so sources need dates.\n3. **Data and login (medium risk):** the three options above. This is the section that decides the approach.\n4. **Candidate widgets (low risk):** e.g. today's todos, upcoming events, a check-in shortcut, mapped to the API endpoints they'd need.\n5. **Opening the app from a widget (low risk):** how a tap opens a specific screen.\n6. **Constraints (low risk):** changes to the web app have to go into `../app` because `frontend/` is a copy; F-Droid build impact (any change to `fdroid/app.solyto.yml` gets flagged); translations; light/dark theming; battery limits; testing.\n7. **Write the report (low risk):** verdict, phased plan, open questions, dated sources.\n\n**Open questions for you:**\n- The brief has no \"Why\" or \"Out of scope\", so the report will suggest candidate widgets rather than pick a final set.\n- Is adding Kotlin to the repo acceptable? Jetpack Glance needs it.\n- Is copying the login token out of the WebView into Android storage acceptable for security and privacy?\n\nThe report will present the last two as trade-offs for you to decide, not assumptions."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3374,"cache_read_input_tokens":31155,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3374},"output_tokens":702,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b01d487b-cfcf-46ad-b278-873bfc9cbb14","uuid":"4623e487-dfd5-48ff-8681-77d5485ffc31","timestamp":"2026-10-15T12:40:44.707Z","request_id":"req_011Cg43CuWmMHLVCVPXTrBhk"}
