, which matches the brief.\n\n**Main finding:** a widget is drawn by Android itself, outside the app, so it can't read the WebView's browser storage. That's where the login token and its expiry date (`auth`) and the server address (`custom_api_url`) are kept. So the main design question is how a widget gets data at all. The report should compare three options:\n- **Snapshot:** the web app sends ready-made widget data to Android through a custom Capacitor plugin, the same way `PullToRefreshPlugin` connects the two today. The widget never contacts the server itself.\n- **Token handoff:** the token is copied into Android storage and the widget fetches data itself, including renewing the token when it expires. This has security implications.\n- **Shortcuts only:** widgets show no data and just open the app.\n\nTapping a widget could open a specific screen the same way shared text already opens `/share` in `MainActivity`.\n\n**Tasks:**\n1. **Current setup (low risk):** list what's already in place: Java vs. Kotlin, Gradle and Android SDK versions, Capacitor plugins, manifest.\n2. **Technical options (medium risk):** compare Android's built-in widget API (`AppWidgetProvider`/`RemoteViews`, no new dependencies), Jetpack Glance (needs Kotlin), and existing Capacitor widget plugins. Library status changes over time, so sources need dates.\n3. **Data and login (medium risk):** the three options above. This is the section that decides the approach.\n4. **Candidate widgets (low risk):** e.g. today's todos, upcoming events, a check-in shortcut, mapped to the API endpoints they'd need.\n5. **Opening the app from a widget (low risk):** how a tap opens a specific screen.\n6. **Constraints (low risk):** changes to the web app have to go into `../app` because `frontend/` is a copy; F-Droid build impact (any change to `fdroid/app.solyto.yml` gets flagged); translations; light/dark theming; battery limits; testing.\n7. **Write the report (low risk):** verdict, phased plan, open questions, dated sources.\n\n**Open questions for you:**\n- The brief has no \"Why\" or \"Out of scope\", so the report will suggest candidate widgets rather than pick a final set.\n- Is adding Kotlin to the repo acceptable? Jetpack Glance needs it.\n- Is copying the login token out of the WebView into Android storage acceptable for security and privacy?\n\nThe report will present the last two as trade-offs for you to decide, not assumptions.","ttft_ms":1411,"type":"result","duration_ms":58998,"uuid":"47a24334-8c4b-4c69-8c90-a2fa4ef44c31","ttft_stream_ms":864,"time_to_request_ms":155,"first_content_frame_ms":864,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}

