{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011CHkanPQsyVRbKU9zudZ7c","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n  \"@capacitor/core\": \">=7.0.0\"\n}\n{\n  \"created\": \"2025-06-03T07:57:00.163Z\",\n  \"modified\": \"2026-03-03T09:05:13.772Z\",\n  \"7.0.0\": \"2025-06-03T07:57:00.415Z\",\n  \"8.0.0\": \"2025-12-29T09:53:07.951Z\",\n  \"8.1.0\": \"2026-03-03T09:05:13.660Z\"\n}\n6:[![Platforms](https://img.shields.io/badge/platforms-iOS%20%7C%20Android-orange)](#-platform-behavior)\n9:A Capacitor plugin to interact with WidgetKit (iOS) and App Widgets (Android).\n10:Allows your Capacitor app to store data in shared user defaults (iOS) or shared preferences (Android),\n17:  <img src=\"androiddemo.gif\" alt=\"Android Example Demo\" width=\"25%\" />\n30:This plugin extends it with Android support and multi-platform improvements. Thank you for the groundwork!\n40:5. Call `WidgetBridgePlugin.reloadAllTimelines()` or `reloadTimelines(...)` after saving data.\n42:### Android\n45:2. Declare them in your `AndroidManifest.xml` with `<receiver ... />`.\n48:   if (Capacitor.getPlatform() === 'android') {\n54:4. Call `WidgetBridgePlugin.setItem(...)` and then `reloadAllTimelines()` or `reloadTimelines(...)` to trigger updates.\n55:5. Use `SharedPreferences` in your widget code to read the data, using the same key/group as in JS.\n64:* [`reloadAllTimelines()`](#reloadalltimelines)\n65:* [`reloadTimelines(...)`](#reloadtimelines)\n85:- Android: Uses SharedPreferences with private app storage.\n107:- Android: Uses SharedPreferences with private app storage.\n129:- Android: Uses SharedPreferences.\n142:### reloadAllTimelines()\n145:reloadAllTimelines() => Promise<DataResults<boolean>>\n148:Reloads timelines for all configured widgets in the app.\n150:- iOS: Triggers WidgetCenter reload.\n151:- Android: Triggers AppWidgetManager update using registered widget class names.\n160:### reloadTimelines(...)\n163:reloadTimelines(options: TimelinesOptions) => Promise<DataResults<boolean>>\n166:Reloads timelines for all widgets of a specified kind.\n168:- iOS: Triggers reload of specific widget kind.\n169:- Android: Triggers update for specific widget kinds if matched in registered widget class names.\n188:Registers widget provider class names for dynamic timeline updates on Android.\n191:- Android: Used to register widget classes for reloadAllTimelines.\n213:- Android: Not supported (returns empty or dummy data).\n231:- Android: Uses AppWidgetManager's `requestPinAppWidget` to prompt the user to add a widget.\n===\n23:* [`reloadAllTimelines()`](#reloadalltimelines)\n24:* [`reloadTimelines(...)`](#reloadtimelines)\n90:### reloadAllTimelines()\n93:reloadAllTimelines() => Promise<DataResults<boolean>>\n96:Reloads the timelines for all configured widgets belonging to the containing app\n105:### reloadTimelines(...)\n108:reloadTimelines(options: TimelinesOptions) => Promise<DataResults<boolean>>\n111:Reloads the timelines for all widgets of a particular kind\n3:Build iOS Home Screen widgets, Lock Screen Live Activities and Android widgets from your Capacitor app, with SVG templates or fully native widget code.\n8:  <p><b>Capgo</b>: push fixes to your Capacitor users in minutes, build signed iOS and Android apps without a Mac, and roll back in one click.</p>\n21:- **SVG template widgets**: `startTemplateWidget()` and `startTemplateActivity()` store layouts for the Home Screen, Lock Screen, Dynamic Island and Android.\n26:- **Platforms**: iOS, Android and Web. Live Activities need ActivityKit on iOS. Web stores state in `localStorage` for development.\n47:- SVG template widgets: store Home Screen, Lock Screen, Dynamic Island, and Android layouts with optional named frames, hotspots, declarative state patches, pause/resume timers, and interaction events. Use this when your widget can be driven by resolved SVG output.\n71:bunx cap sync android\n91:The plugin ships the native pieces a widget extension or Android widget can use:\n99:- `CapgoTemplateActionReceiver` and `CapgoTemplateWidgetBridge` for Android template widgets\n153:This mode is for Home Screen, Lock Screen, Dynamic Island, and Android widgets that can render resolved SVG. Hotspot actions can switch frames, mutate state, pause/play timers, and emit events for the app to process later.\nShell cwd was reset to /workspace","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e434ac5a-b708-42d2-a42c-74ecdd5e76a8","uuid":"58b15303-a902-40fb-9bdf-d0afb9ad991b","timestamp":"2026-10-15T12:41:52.189Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\n  \"@capacitor/core\": \">=7.0.0\"\n}\n{\n  \"created\": \"2025-06-03T07:57:00.163Z\",\n  \"modified\": \"2026-03-03T09:05:13.772Z\",\n  \"7.0.0\": \"2025-06-03T07:57:00.415Z\",\n  \"8.0.0\": \"2025-12-29T09:53:07.951Z\",\n  \"8.1.0\": \"2026-03-03T09:05:13.660Z\"\n}\n6:[![Platforms](https://img.shields.io/badge/platforms-iOS%20%7C%20Android-orange)](#-platform-behavior)\n9:A Capacitor plugin to interact with WidgetKit (iOS) and App Widgets (Android).\n10:Allows your Capacitor app to store data in shared user defaults (iOS) or shared preferences (Android),\n17:  <img src=\"androiddemo.gif\" alt=\"Android Example Demo\" width=\"25%\" />\n30:This plugin extends it with Android support and multi-platform improvements. Thank you for the groundwork!\n40:5. Call `WidgetBridgePlugin.reloadAllTimelines()` or `reloadTimelines(...)` after saving data.\n42:### Android\n45:2. Declare them in your `AndroidManifest.xml` with `<receiver ... />`.\n48:   if (Capacitor.getPlatform() === 'android') {\n54:4. Call `WidgetBridgePlugin.setItem(...)` and then `reloadAllTimelines()` or `reloadTimelines(...)` to trigger updates.\n55:5. Use `SharedPreferences` in your widget code to read the data, using the same key/group as in JS.\n64:* [`reloadAllTimelines()`](#reloadalltimelines)\n65:* [`reloadTimelines(...)`](#reloadtimelines)\n85:- Android: Uses SharedPreferences with private app storage.\n107:- Android: Uses SharedPreferences with pri