{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg43gDgffgX9NUiL3nDVx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written the audit to `docs/reports/android-homescreen-widgets.md`. The short answer is that home-screen widgets are feasible with the current setup, and the cheapest version needs no new dependencies and no change to the F-Droid recipe. No code, build files, `frontend/` or `fdroid/` were touched, and the worktree is clean.\n\nThe recommendation is a direction for you to confirm, not a decision:\n- **How to build them:** use Android's built-in widget API (`AppWidgetProvider` + `RemoteViews`) in Java, the same language as the existing native code.\n- **Why not the alternatives:** Jetpack Glance has a nicer API but needs Kotlin and Compose, which the repo doesn't have today. I checked the community Capacitor widget plugins on npm and in their published packages. None ships ready-made Android widgets, one is iOS-only, and the best-maintained one requires Capacitor 8 (we're on 7).\n- **Where the data comes from:** this is the hard part. The login token and API URL live in the WebView's `localStorage`, which native code can't read. The recommended route is that the web app pushes a small ready-to-display snapshot to native storage, so the widget never holds the token. The catch is the data is only as fresh as the last time the app was open.\n- **Phasing:**\n  - **First:** a shortcut widget with buttons into Todos, Calendar, Notes and so on. It needs no data and no web-app change.\n  - **Second:** a read-only \"Your Day\" widget (today's and overdue todos plus today's events). It closely matches the existing dashboard component.\n  - **Only after a decision on copying the token into native storage:** widgets that change data, like tick-off-a-todo or start/stop a timer.\n\nAny JavaScript change (the snapshot push, clearing it on logout, a \"quick add\" route) has to be made in `../app`, limited to the mobile build (`IS_MOBILE`).\n\nVersions, licences and deprecations come from npm, Google's Maven repository and the Android docs, all checked today and listed with dates in the sources section.\n\n**Decisions for you** (all listed in the report's open questions):\n- Which widgets to ship. The report lists nine candidates with rough effort but doesn't pick.\n- Whether adding Kotlin (needed for Glance) is acceptable.\n- Whether copying the login token out of the WebView into native storage is acceptable for security and privacy.\n- Whether data widgets should hide details by default, since anyone looking at an unlocked phone sees them.\n\n**Not verified:**\n- Whether the web app can call a custom native plugin through the `window.Capacitor` global without adding `@capacitor/core` as a dependency. Testing this would need a small prototype, which was out of scope.\n- Whether refreshing a token invalidates the old one on the server. This matters for the token option, and it can't be answered from this repo because the backend lives elsewhere.\n\n**Unrelated finding:** the manifest accepts `app.solyto://` links, but nothing in the app handles them, so they open the app without going to any particular page. That may affect the email-verification and password-reset links that point back into the app. This is noted as a follow-up in `implementation.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1596,"cache_read_input_tokens":87881,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1596},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e434ac5a-b708-42d2-a42c-74ecdd5e76a8","uuid":"e46613e1-9751-4a5b-8aa1-6241a07f3f75","timestamp":"2026-10-15T12:46:58.688Z","request_id":"req_011Cg43gCw2S9dzFXAKgsrhv"}
