ther data widgets should hide details by default, since anyone looking at an unlocked phone sees them.\n\n**Not verified:**\n- Whether the web app can call a custom native plugin through the `window.Capacitor` global without adding `@capacitor/core` as a dependency. Testing this would need a small prototype, which was out of scope.\n- Whether refreshing a token invalidates the old one on the server. This matters for the token option, and it can't be answered from this repo because the backend lives elsewhere.\n\n**Unrelated finding:** the manifest accepts `app.solyto://` links, but nothing in the app handles them, so they open the app without going to any particular page. That may affect the email-verification and password-reset links that point back into the app. This is noted as a follow-up in `implementation.md`.","ttft_ms":2783,"type":"result","duration_ms":370667,"uuid":"386dc0c6-f2b5-49cf-a470-63ccfedef461","ttft_stream_ms":986,"time_to_request_ms":120,"first_content_frame_ms":987,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}

