 the app at a specific route (PendingIntent → `MainActivity` → `loadUrl(\"https://my.solyto.app/<route>\")`, the same approach as `handleShareIntent`), including the `singleTask`/`onNewIntent` behaviour.\n  files (read-only): android/app/src/main/java/app/solyto/MainActivity.java, android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml; output in report\n  depends: TASK-1\n  risk: low. The pattern already exists in the code.\n\nTASK-6: Assess cross-cutting impact and constraints: vendored-frontend workflow (JS changes go to `../app`, gated on `IS_MOBILE`), F-Droid build implications (new Gradle deps, Kotlin plugin, reproducibility, `fdroid/app.solyto.yml` flagged), i18n (widget strings in Android `res/values-*` for en/de/fr/es versus the web i18n tables), light/dark theming with the existing `colors.xml`, battery and update-frequency limits, and testing approach.\n  files (read-only): scripts/build-fdroid.sh, scripts/vendor.sh, fdroid/app.solyto.yml, .github/workflows/release.yml, android/app/src/main/res/values/colors.xml; output in report\n  depends: TASK-2, TASK-3\n  risk: low. It is analysis only, but any recommendation that would change `fdroid/app.solyto.yml` must be flagged.\n\nTASK-7: Write the final report `docs/reports/android-homescreen-widgets.md`. It should contain: a summary/verdict (feasible yes/no and recommended approach), current state (TASK-1), options comparison (TASK-2), data/auth (TASK-3), candidate widgets (TASK-4), deep linking (TASK-5), constraints and risks (TASK-6), a phased rough plan (for example an MVP shortcut widget, then a data widget), open questions for the maintainer, and dated sources.\n  files: docs/reports/android-homescreen-widgets.md (new)\n  depends: TASK-2, TASK-3, TASK-4, TASK-5, TASK-6\n  risk: low. It is documentation only, with no build or runtime impact.\n\n## Unclear / for the maintainer\n\n- The brief has no \"Why\" and no \"Out of scope\". The analyst assumes the\n  report stays technology-agnostic about *which* widgets ship. It proposes\n  candidates and does not pick a final set.\n- It is unclear whether introducing Kotlin (needed for Glance) is acceptable\n  in this repo. The report should present this as a trade-off, not assume it.\n- It is unclear whether moving the auth token out of the WebView into native\n  storage is acceptable from a security/privacy standpoint. The report\n  should surface this as a decision for the maintainer.\n# Implementation: Audit: android homescreen widgets\n\nid: opinion\ndeveloper: @developer\ndate: 2026-10-15\n\n## Summary\n\nThis job produced one report, `docs/reports/android-homescreen-widgets.md`,\nand no code, build, manifest, `patch/`, `frontend/` or `fdroid/` changes.\n\nVerdict: widgets are feasible. The recommended approach is Java\n`AppWidgetProvider` + `RemoteViews`. Start with a static shortcut widget,\nthen add a read-only \"Your Day\" widget fed by a snapshot that the web app\npushes over a small custom bridge, so the token never leaves the WebView.\nInteractive widgets come only after the maintainer decides on the token.\nThe report lists these as recommendations and open questions; it does not\nmake the decisions.\n\n## Changes\n\nAll tasks wrote to `docs/reports/android-homescreen-widgets.md` (new file;\nthe `docs/reports/` directory was created by writing it). Tasks 1–7 were\ncommitted together in one commit because they are sections of a single\ndocument.\n\nTASK-1: §2 \"Current state\". Inventory of Java/AGP 8.13.0/Gradle 8.14.3,\nSDK 24/36/36, AndroidX deps, Capacitor 7 with no npm plugins, the\n`PullToRefreshPlugin` bridge pattern, manifest/intents, colours, strings\nand tests.\nTASK-2: §3. Comparison of RemoteViews (+ `core-remoteviews` backport),\nGlance (1.2.0 stable, needs Kotlin + Compose compiler) and community\nplugins (checked on npm with tarballs inspected; none fits Capacitor 7\nwell). Includes API 31 constraints.\nTASK-3: §4. Three data/auth options (snapshot push, token handoff +\nWorkManager, static), the token-refresh conflict, security-crypto\ndeprecation (verified from release notes) versus AndroidKeyStore, backup\nrules, and privacy.\nTASK-4: §5. Nine candidate widgets mapped to `apiRoutes` keys and routes,\nwith interaction needs and complexity for each data option.\nTASK-5: §6. PendingIntent → `MainActivity` (`singleTask`,\n`onCreate`/`onNewIntent`) → `loadUrl`, modelled on `handleShareIntent`,\nwith a route allowlist and `FLAG_IMMUTABLE`.\nTASK-6: §7. Vendored workflow (`../app`, `IS_MOBILE`), F-Droid impact\n(no `fdroid/app.solyto.yml` change for the recommended path; Glance is\nflagged), i18n, theming, battery and testing.\nTASK-7: Summary/verdict, phased plan, open questions and dated sources.\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n- Not verified (it would need a spike): whether\n  `window.Capacitor.Plugins.<Name>` works for a custom plugin without\n  `@capacitor/core` bundled in the web app. This is listed as an open\n  question.\n- Backend behaviour can't be determined from this repo: whether token\n  refresh invalidates the old token, revocation, and token lifetime.\n- Side observation, out of scope: the manifest declares a `VIEW\n  app.solyto://` intent filter, but there is no native handler and no\n  `@capacitor/app`, so these deep links only open the app and don't\n  navigate anywhere. It may be worth checking whether the auth verify/reset\n  deep links (`getDeepLinkUrl`) behave as intended.\n# Verdict: Audit: android homescreen widgets\n\nid: opinion\nreviewer:\ndate:\n\n<!-- Produced by @reviewer and/or @security after implementation. -->\n\n## Review\n\n<!-- TASK-1: PASS / FAIL / PARTIAL\n     notes: ...\n\nTASK-2: ...\n-->\n\n## Security\n\n<!-- Any security findings from @security, or \"none\" if not run. -->\n\n## Overall\n\n<!-- APPROVED / REJECTED / NEEDS WORK -->\n<!-- Summary of what needs to change before this can be approved, if anything. -->\nls: cannot access '/workspace/.manigot': No such file or directory\nbaf0513 [opinion] chore: commit all\n9586b29 [opinion] implementation: add summary\nf1edce9 [opinion] TASK-1..7: add Android home-screen widgets audit report\n2327ad5 [opinion] chore: commit all\n7947752 [opinion] chore: commit all\n71367c7 Scaffold job opinion_audit-android-homescreen-widgets\n63025df Swipe from top to reload\n4d4fd47 mg init\n .../brief.md                                       |  24 +\n .../implementation.md                              |  61 +++\n .../session.log                                    | 247 ++++++++++\n .../tasks.md                                       |  94 ++++\n .../tokens.json                                    |  26 ++\n .../verdict.md                                     |  24 +\n docs/reports/android-homescreen-widgets.md         | 514 +++++++++++++++++++++\n 7 files changed, 990 insertions(+)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01PPqtG8dAiKFtHgNSFUyEja","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
