{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg43jcbuGy3Q9yiPcRU9Q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I approved the job. All seven tasks pass and nothing needs to change before merge. The verdict is committed as `2582f4e`.\n\n**What changed:** the only change outside the job's own files is the new report, `docs/reports/android-homescreen-widgets.md`. There are no code, Gradle, manifest, `patch/`, `frontend/` or `fdroid/` changes, which is what the report-only scope asked for. I diffed against `main` because there's no `.manigot/manigot.json` setting a different base.\n\n**What the report concludes:** widgets are feasible. It recommends the plain Android widget API in Java, with no new dependencies, no Kotlin and no change to the F-Droid recipe. A widget that shows data would get it as a snapshot pushed by the web app, so the login token never leaves the WebView. It leaves the real decisions open for you: which widgets to ship, whether to add Kotlin, and whether to copy the token into native storage.\n\n**What I checked:** the report's claims about this repo all match the code. That covers:\n- build versions and SDK levels, and the manifest contents;\n- how login is stored and refreshed (key `auth`, 14-day/5-day threshold);\n- the API route names and the existing app routes;\n- the `/share` redirect when `q` is missing;\n- F-Droid's `UpdateCheckMode: Tags`.\n\n**Not verified:**\n- I didn't re-check the outside package versions, licences and dates (npm, Google Maven, Android docs). Those come from the developer's own research, which lists dated sources.\n- Two things the report itself leaves as open questions, correctly in my view:\n  - whether a custom plugin can be called from the web app without adding `@capacitor/core` (needs a small test build);\n  - whether refreshing a token on the server invalidates the old one (the backend isn't in this repo).\n\n**Minor, not blocking:** inside the data section, the options are numbered 3.1–3.3. Those numbers clash with the §3.1–3.3 technology headings earlier in the report, which can make cross-references confusing.\n\n**Separate issue the developer raised:** the manifest accepts `app.solyto://` links, and `@capacitor/app` isn't installed. The developer says nothing in the Java code handles these links, so they would open the app without going to the intended page. That could affect the email verify and password-reset links. I didn't read `MainActivity` to confirm the missing handler. It's outside this job, but probably worth checking."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1930,"cache_read_input_tokens":39445,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1930},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b9984020-1b19-4dab-ae92-05719b25550a","uuid":"55878fe7-9bbf-4da2-b964-c21b32d19a77","timestamp":"2026-10-15T12:47:43.869Z","request_id":"req_011Cg43jcKXy83fcJzCMjRiW"}
